<title>USA: Genrad Inc Q1 oper EPS rises before item.</title>
<headline>Genrad Inc Q1 oper EPS rises before item.</headline>
<dateline>CONCORD, Mass. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q1 - Three Months Ended</p>
<p>				Mar 29, 1997   Mar 30, 1996  % change</p>
<p> Orders			$ 61,266,000   $ 48,270,000	27%</p>
<p> Total Sales		   52,500,000     43,554,000	21%</p>
<p> Net Income		    11,717,000	6,949,000	69%</p>
<p> EPS-Primary			   0.42	     0.30	40%</p>
<p> EPS-Fully Diluted		   0.42	     0.29	45%</p>
<p> Shrs-Primary		  28,106,000     23,256,000	21%</p>
<p> Shrs-Fully Diluted	  28,106,000     26,984,000	 4%</p>
<p> Net Excluding Tax Benefit  6,329,000	4,469,000	42%</p>
<p> Interest on Convertible debt $     -	  933,000</p>
<p>Net Income Adjusted to Calculated</p>
<p>   Fully diluted EPS	  6,329,000	5,402,000	17%</p>
<p>Per Share Data - Fully Diluted:</p>
<p> Net Income as Reported	    0.42	     0.29	45%</p>
<p> Tax Benefit			  (0.19)	   (0.09)</p>
<p> Net Excluding Tax Benefit	 0.23	     0.20	15%</p>
<p>Note: The tax benefit is due to a reduction in the company's deferred tax asset valuation allowance.</p>
</text>
